{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786659668612483001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"buried-genial-gyrfalcon","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":5,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"2cdb07c4ece8497d68efc8b8f23714d59989adec05722d5c6d8b8e9ebfb8518f","event_uuid":"3615450d-b2f8-4b84-abf8-6d5ff7293363","position":{"commit_sha":"5db696ed90694b6b689c8f17c6689b5d42bbe7c8","position":"1786160092828819001-3615450d-b2f8-4b84-abf8-6d5ff7293363"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6bf1704e3ad4459f536a63537017c0e95a600ba99681f941d8f0f84305ad48a1","event_uuid":"25a57098-997a-4ea9-b998-b2aacd2ab59e","position":{"commit_sha":"e1477ef5312320baccbf424aadf7c29d5d4e9f58","position":"1786160166557576001-25a57098-997a-4ea9-b998-b2aacd2ab59e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ed31360e8d5052833366dcd5661204ac462317c096a8b0844761612c66a5dbe3","event_uuid":"e5126afa-a2a7-4d13-93e7-4f32f5e9650d","position":{"commit_sha":"caa56f8f6d7d1a9210e338c5bf0ec7c68e5d30c2","position":"1786160200053318001-e5126afa-a2a7-4d13-93e7-4f32f5e9650d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8242c05f36700cb860b5bdc0c4ddf8ad2eddd740f3cb15713012c60d7dd39d96","event_uuid":"2ea28a84-9880-4e3c-b2f0-7fcdbcf23558","position":{"commit_sha":"d2c8ba272930509aab5af91ab0860a163508939f","position":"1786162247650851001-2ea28a84-9880-4e3c-b2f0-7fcdbcf23558"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ed16a52b26064b6ce30e517ea3dfc5bd0fc08c8ac95009090923dcd84bed7d27","event_uuid":"a8e248aa-3681-464b-98e8-8a4cd05accff","position":{"commit_sha":"59d1050ab2745e86b6833d33d96f1436143857de","position":"1786162253238959001-a8e248aa-3681-464b-98e8-8a4cd05accff"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786160092828819001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e5126afa-a2a7-4d13-93e7-4f32f5e9650d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"c927-0a68-4465-42a2"},{"link_uuid":"2ea28a84-9880-4e3c-b2f0-7fcdbcf23558","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"4631-5598-7127-4a56"},{"link_uuid":"a8e248aa-3681-464b-98e8-8a4cd05accff","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ce02-47ed-6505-4925"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA rebar ticket carries no record of which tracker project it syncs into, nor which repos it belongs\nto. The current ticket state fields are seeded in `src/rebar/reducer/_state.py:29-81` and declared in\n`src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`; neither includes a project. Today the project is only\nimplicit — recoverable from a bound issue's key prefix in `bindings.json`, and absent entirely for a\nticket that has never been bound. Epic `0e68-41eb-5782-4336` needs it explicit, because a ticket that\nis deliberately not synced has no binding to infer from.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd two ticket state fields together, in one edit set: `bridge_project` (string) and `repos` (list of\nstrings). They are one story rather than two because a field is not usable without its write path,\nand splitting them would put two children on `src/rebar/_commands/composer.py`.\n\n`bridge_project` is **tri-state**, mirroring the established `file_impact_scope`\nundeclared/none/paths pattern (`docs/ticket-model.md:210-212`): absent means legacy, an explicit\nempty string means never sync, and a key means sync there. The three states are distinguished so a\npre-feature store is not read as \"every ticket is unsynced\". Resolution of the absent state is not\nimplemented here — it belongs to `resolve_project` in the mapping module.\n\nBoth fields are written into the CREATE event data by `create_core`\n(`src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:169-220`), projected by the reducer, and seeded in\n`make_initial_state`. Create-time arguments `--bridge-project` and `--repos` are added to all three\nwrite surfaces — CLI (`composer.create_cli`), library (`src/rebar/_lib_writes.py:79-135`), and MCP\n(`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:47-70`). Note the CLI flag loop rejects unknown options strictly\n(`composer.py:287-291`), so the new flags must be registered there or they are hard errors.\n\n`bridge_project` is **promote-only**: setting it on a ticket with no binding is allowed, changing it\non a ticket that already holds one is refused. That keeps the change free of any issue-move or\nunbind/rebind machinery. `repos` stays freely editable — it never reaches the tracker, so there is no\nbinding to invalidate.\n\nNo schema version bump: `docs/event-schema.md:124-150` states additive fields on an existing event\ntype do not require one. Types are generated from the schemas (`reducer/_state.py:11-13`), so the\ngenerator is re-run.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json`\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_state.py`\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`\n- `src/rebar/_commands/composer.py`\n- `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py`\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`\n- tests under `tests/`\n\n## Testing\n\nTier per the shared standard: a producer/consumer contract test for the event→state path (real\nCREATE event fed through the real reducer, no stubbing), plus a real CLI subprocess test for the\nargument parsing, since the strict unknown-option rejection is itself part of the mechanism.\n\n- Happy path: `create task \"t\" --bridge-project REB --repos rebar,api` produces a ticket whose state\n  shows `bridge_project == \"REB\"` and `repos == [\"rebar\", \"api\"]` after a full replay.\n- Three-state coverage: a ticket created without the flag replays with the field **absent**; one\n  created with an explicit empty value replays with `\"\"`. These must be distinguishable — asserting\n  the absent case is not merely falsy is the point of the test.\n- Cross-surface parity: the same ticket shape results from the CLI, the library, and MCP.\n- Failure path: an edit setting `bridge_project` on a ticket that already holds a binding is refused\n  with a non-zero exit and the stored value is unchanged; the same edit on an unbound ticket succeeds.\n- Collateral invariant: replaying a ticket created before this change yields identical state apart\n  from the two new keys.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `bridge_project` and `repos` are declared in the ticket state schema, seeded in\n      `make_initial_state`, and projected by the reducer; checked by a replay test asserting both on\n      a freshly created ticket.\n- [ ] `--bridge-project` and `--repos` exist on the CLI, library and MCP create paths and produce\n      identical state; checked by a per-surface test comparing the resulting ticket state.\n- [ ] The absent, explicit-empty, and set states are distinguishable after replay; checked by a\n      parameterized test asserting each of the three separately.\n- [ ] Setting `bridge_project` on a bound ticket is refused while setting it on an unbound ticket\n      succeeds; checked by a paired test covering both directions.\n- [ ] A ticket created before this change replays to the same state apart from the new keys; checked\n      by a fixture-based regression test.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/ticket_state.schema.json","reason":"declare bridge_project and repos"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_state.py","reason":"seed both fields in initial state"},{"path":"src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py","reason":"project both fields from the CREATE event"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/composer.py","reason":"CREATE event data and the create-time CLI arguments"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_writes.py","reason":"library create parity for the new arguments"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py","reason":"MCP create parity for the new arguments"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ticket_project_fields.py","reason":"three-state replay, cross-surface parity, promote-only rule"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","4631-5598-7127-4a56"],["depends_on","c927-0a68-4465-42a2"],["depends_on","ce02-47ed-6505-4925"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3","ticket_type":"story","title":"Ticket fields: tri-state bridge_project and repos, with create-time arguments on all three write surfaces","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3615450d-b2f8-4b84-abf8-6d5ff7293363","25a57098-997a-4ea9-b998-b2aacd2ab59e","e5126afa-a2a7-4d13-93e7-4f32f5e9650d","2ea28a84-9880-4e3c-b2f0-7fcdbcf23558","a8e248aa-3681-464b-98e8-8a4cd05accff"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659668612483001,"uuid":"8f6690e7-bcbc-4998-99cf-85ee9d70ec84"}